  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $\\log _{2}\\left(x^{2}+2 x-1\\right)=1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\log _{2}\\left(x^{2}+2 x-1\\right)=\\log _{2} 2$\r\n$\\Rightarrow$ $x^{2}+2 x-1=2$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad x^{2}+2 x-3=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad x^{2}+3 x-x-3=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad x(x+3)-1(x+3)=0$\r\n$=(x+3)(x-1)=0$\r\n$x=1,-3$\r\nSince, $x=1$ and $x=-3$ are satisfy the given equation therefore the number of solutions of the equation are two.",
